# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository and in every working copy.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the default on GitHub's Windows runners)
# rewrites every file to CRLF, and the `.alethic/` fixtures stop parsing — which is exactly how CI
# failed while the same commit was green on a Windows machine whose working copy still held LF.
# The parser now tolerates CRLF on its own; this keeps the bytes consistent so diffs stay clean and
# nobody debugs an invisible whitespace difference between two machines.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.wasm binary
